#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid "What's included:"
msgstr ""

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
#, python-format
msgid ""
"<strong>An account on %(product_name)s <a href=\"%(login_url)s\" "
"target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">platform</a></strong> for the duration of "
"this course. Every prompt is a real, billable request to an LLM provider, so "
"please experiment freely, but don't run automated load against it."
msgstr ""

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid ""
"<strong>Your own AI resources.</strong> You can create, change and delete "
"your own LLMClients, plugins, connections and secrets, and you are "
"encouraged to experiment with them while you are attending this course."
msgstr ""

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid ""
"<strong>Thousands of LLMs from nine providers:</strong> Anthropic, Cohere, "
"Fireworks AI, Google AI (Gemini), Hugging Face, Meta AI (Llama), Mistral, "
"OpenAI and Together AI, all through a single interface, so that you can "
"compare models hands-on."
msgstr ""

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid ""
"<strong><a href=\"https://docs.smarter.sh/smarter-resources/smarter-"
"llmtool.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Plugins</a> for LLM tool "
"calling</strong> that connect an LLM to SQL databases, remote REST APIs, web "
"search, image search, Agent Skills and static data. Your data stays where it "
"is: the LLM only sees the query results and responses that it asks for. <a "
"href=\"https://docs.smarter.sh/smarter-framework/smarter-extensions.html\" "
"rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Extensions</a>, which the platform "
"administrator installs, add tools written in Python."
msgstr ""

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
#, python-format
msgid ""
"<strong>A no-code approach to authoring AI resources.</strong> Every "
"resource in %(product_name)s is a short <a href=\"https://docs.smarter.sh/"
"smarter-framework/smarter-manifests.html\" rel=\"noopener\" "
"target=\"_blank\">YAML manifest</a>, so you can build and manage a working "
"AI application without writing code."
msgstr ""

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid ""
"<strong>A web Prompt Engineering Workbench</strong> for designing, testing "
"and debugging the prompts of your AI applications interactively."
msgstr ""

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
msgid "Open Source, Built for Production"
msgstr ""

#: smarter/templates/account/email/welcome.html
#, python-format
msgid ""
"<strong>%(product_name)s is more than a teaching tool.</strong> It is free, "
"open source software, licensed under the GNU AGPL v3, and it was built to "
"run in production: on Kubernetes, with cost accounting, secrets management "
"and per-account access control. Running at scale, security and cost "
"management may be out of scope for this course, but you will face them once "
"you complete it, and the source code and documentation are there for you to "
"explore, during the course and after."
msgstr ""

